{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/110386-lunars-changing-themselves-to-change-the-world","id":110386,"title":"\"Lunars changing themselves to change the world\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-10T16:19:44-07:00","id":110386,"title":"\"Lunars changing themselves to change the world\"?","content":"Other than the one at Chancel Aleph, can anyone find a developer quote claiming that Lunar Exalted in Third Edition will have a theme of changing themselves to change the world?<br /> <br /> I ask because I'm confused; it seems like a dubious theme at which to aim with the Lunar Exalted, considering the developers plan to simultaneously aim for &quot;primal god, mythic monster&quot; and scale back <i>away </i>from &quot;fleshy monstrosity&quot;.<br /> <br /> A splat with a theme of physicality, and one which focuses primarily on internal changes to work magic, would seem to demand a &quot;Zerg swarm&quot; sort of aesthetic -- an organic parallel to the Alchemical Exalted, with Charms being physical organs and limbs developed through deliberate genetic manipulation. This is rather what I expect from the organ-and-limb associated Liminal Exalted, minus the potential to become sprawling complexes made from meat and synapses.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, internal chemistry/alchemy with a <i>spiritual </i>slant is where the Getimians are going, with their inner Pattern Spiders and Yin/Yang mote pools.<br /> <br /> Finally, an internal focus would seem to exclude some previous Lunar Charm concepts which seem rather important to them. The ability to transform others into animals, for example, or to disfigure people with scars magically charged with emotion and meaning, or to paint their mark on a Wyld impossibility to bring it back safely into Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T16:29:53-07:00","id":110394,"title":"","content":"Changing themselves to change the world sounds just like what Lunars have always done in Exalted. I don't think that needs to be interpreted to mean anything reductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T17:14:23-07:00","id":110416,"title":"","content":"Didn't that quote say changing themselves <i>rather</i> than changing the world?<br /> <br /> My intuitive approach to this is something like: Solars change the world, having Charms like Taboo-Inflicting Diatribe to expand on their capacity to relate to people on guide social ideas in order to entrench expansive new social drives that work are adopted primarily because the Solar says they should be (even though, should they lack a hook for people's motivations, they'll be dropped not long after the Solar stops talking).<br /> <br /> Lunars change themselves; they have Charms to become beautiful, fearsome things, things that people respond to in particular ways because of what they are rather than what they do.<br /> <br /> It might be somewhat poor form to use Solar effects to establish Lunar methods, but without a firm basis for particular Lunar effects, I would say it's a matter of difference of people staying away from a place because a Solar made a very compelling argument to do so, and staying away because a Lunar is living there in the form of a terrible thing.<br /> <br /> I feel like there could be other elements, elements not produced directly by Charms but by things informed by (and that inform) Charms; things like when John talks about his Sidereal character being a strong guiding influence on a Solar without having Charms that do that, because the context and nature of Sidereals gives them a drive and a qualification to so guide Solars.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's part of an idea that a Solar swordsman might change the world because, even if they're only good at fighting stuff, there'll be people who orient their policies and responses around the reality that there's a person who's really good at killing stuff walking through the area.<br /> <br /> A Lunar warrior is more... between how they kill, and reputations and realities about their personality (like their temper), people tend to want to stay out of their way, let them get on with their business, move on, and then try to keep things business as usual, maybe try to rebuild in the wake of them.<br /> <br /> Between their conduct and their aesthetic, a Solar warrior is somebody who draws attention, even some manner of desire to exploit. A Lunar warrior might have the opposite effect; people don't want to catch their eyes for fear of becoming their next target.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although there might be a simpler thing to it, an idea about perspective and motivation.<br /> <br /> It might be that Solars <i>feel</i> powerful, they feel more powerful than anything, and even if they weren't likely often Chosen from people who would be motivated to use such power to make things different, it can be hard not to challenge great things when you feel more powerful than they are, and hard not to create sweeping changes when you beat them.<br /> <br /> It might be that Lunars feel like they can adjust themselves to continue fitting in with the world that changes around them, or adjust themselves into a thing that the world has to keep up with. This doesn't mean that Lunars are cringingly keeping their heads low, or never fight great things, but... their inclinations might be directed less towards changing how things are going on, and more about keeping themselves competitive in that arena, even adopting the role and place of things they tear down.<br /> <br /> I often like to refer to the idea of Demetheus incidentally defeating a mighty raksha prince; it could be that a Lunar in that scenario would have a stronger inclination to then go back to the raksha's palace and start living it up in their place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-10-2014, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T17:28:37-07:00","id":110425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/110386-lunars-changing-themselves-to-change-the-world?p=110416#post110416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't that quote say changing themselves <i>rather</i> than changing the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>It did indeed.<br /> <br /> And I can see how that can be interpreted to mean that Lunar Exalted are better about changing themselves without meaning that they are <i>incapable</i> of affecting external changes... just notably inferior to Solars in that regard.<br /> <br /> Just having alternative true forms and Heart's Blood shapeshifting automatically makes the Lunars weighted towards personal change than outward affect, and that's before getting into personal shapeshifting Charms or Knacks. A Lunar's best and most versatile tool is almost always his own body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might be somewhat poor form to use Solar effects to establish Lunar methods, but without a firm basis for particular Lunar effects, I would say it's a matter of difference of people staying away from a place because a Solar made a very compelling argument to do so, and staying away because a Lunar is living there in the form of a terrible thing. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I hope that Perfect Fear Scent makes a return in some form, so that Lunars can use words alone to make people fear a thing, whether it's present or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like there could be other elements, elements not produced directly by Charms but by things informed by (and that inform) Charms; things like when John talks about his Sidereal character being a strong guiding influence on a Solar without having Charms that do that, because the context and nature of Sidereals gives them a drive and a qualification to so guide Solars.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's part of an idea that a Solar swordsman might change the world because, even if they're only good at fighting stuff, there'll be people who orient their policies and responses around the reality that there's a person who's really good at killing stuff walking through the area.<br /> <br /> A Lunar warrior is more... between how they kill, and reputations and realities about their personality (like their temper), people tend to want to stay out of their way, let them get on with their business, move on, and then try to keep things business as usual, maybe try to rebuild in the wake of them.<br /> <br /> Between their conduct and their aesthetic, a Solar warrior is somebody who draws attention, even some manner of desire to exploit. A Lunar warrior might have the opposite effect; people don't want to catch their eyes for fear of becoming their next target. </div> </div> </div>Seems so. Lunars are just inescapably more inhuman than Solars. Those who seek to exploit Solars are more likely to find Solar methods comfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}